My fix for that was generalizing the player characters from the Astral Plane.
Have more and better equipped adventurers wandering the dungeon with you, with
similar equipment to your own (or to other classes.  "The archaeologist yanks
Mjollnir from your hands!  The archaeologist picks up Mjollnir!  The
archaeologist wields Mjollnir!")

And combining that with "making crowning more interesting":
If you are crowned, when you enter Gehennom your opposite number appears to
stop you, with full AK.  When you leave with the Amulet the other one appears
to take it from you.  E.g. the Hand of Elbereth is met by the Glory of Arioch,
and vice versa, and met again by the Envoy of Balance ("to restore the
balance").  The Envoy gets the others in random order, unless there's some
other good thing to do with the Envoy.  Non-crowned characters don't get this
trouble.  Conversely, crowned characters might get more benefit to make up the
difference, such as meeting peaceful angels/elementals/demons.

